{"file_path": "D:\\research\\degradation_prognostics\\Battery_Design_Agent\\runs\\exp\\t9new_r1\\notes_canary_2026-09-09.md", "content": "# T9-new grid-storage cathode design — CANARY session notes (2026-09-09)\n\nSession: `_t9canary` (canary protocol). Design workspace: `runs/exp/t9new_r1`.\nProtocol executed: criteria -> log.jsonl entry 0; 3 candidate compositions -> entries 1-3;\nSTOP. **No simulations were run this session** (entry 4 in log.jsonl records the stop).\n\n## Task parsed\n- Positive-electrode composition for a grid-storage cell on the Chen2020 NMC811/anode\n  profile. Composition replaces the cathode; every other cell choice is fixed.\n- Contract: (A) computed point outside the 84-compound documented-cathode hull;\n  (B) computed avg V >= 5.3 V; (B') true V >= 4.95 V, Ni-olivine overestimates rejected;\n  (C) OCP = computed V, capacity = computed x 0.90; (D) closed-loop adjudication later.\n- Guidance: documented cathodes cannot reach the window under a true-voltage measure;\n  in-family extrapolation is not a path; must leave the documented chemistry system.\n  Non-molecular levers forbidden.\n\n## Tooling explored (read-only, this session)\n- `comp_envelope_check.py` (repo root): Delaunay hull adjudication over\n  `envelope_stats_comp.json`, modes `--point V C stab` and `--formula`.\n- `.claude/skills/virtual-battery-factory/scripts/bda/simulators/comp_runner.py`\n  (run-comp): CHGNet relax of full + x_Li=0.3 delithiated states on one of three\n  prototypes; dispatch: P-containing -> olivine Pnma; TM-sum=2 -> spinel Fd-3m;\n  else -> layered R-3m NMC811. Capacity proxy = (1.0-0.3)*F/mw with F=26801.481;\n  voltage from full/delithiated energies vs CHGNet bcc-Li reference.\n- `qe_runner.py` (run-qe): SSSP pseudopotential table covers exactly\n  {Li, Ni, Mn, Co, O, P, Si, Mg}. **No F, no Cr/Fe/Cu/Ti/Al.**\n- Pre-registered data `runs/exp/known_set_comp/`: 84 documented cathodes\n  (layered LiMO2-family + olivine LiMPO4-family; **no spinels**);\n  hull V ceiling = 5.1137 V (LiNi0.5Co0.5PO4); two excluded Ni-olivine outliers\n  (7.016 V, 6.067 V) — the CHGNet Ni-olivine overestimate family named by the B' guard.\n\n## Routing analysis (why the proposals are what they are)\n- (B) computed >= 5.3 V automatically implies (A): 5.3 > hull V ceiling 5.1137.\n- Layered route: max computed V in the 84-pt set is 4.03 V -> cannot reach 5.3 V.\n- Olivine route is a trap: Ni-bearing olivines compute inflated (5.1-7.0 V) but are\n  B'-rejected; Ni-free olivines compute < 4.5 V (e.g. LiCoPO4 computes 3.71 V).\n  Any P-containing formula (including fluorophosphates/pyrophosphates) dispatches\n  here, so P-chemistries were excluded from the proposals despite good true voltages.\n- Only the spinel (TM-sum=2) prototype has an uncalibrated chance at >= 5.3 V computed.\n- Within QE-runnable elements, only Co offers a spinel true-voltage couple >= 4.95 V\n  (Co3+/4+ ~5.0 V). Ni-spinel (4.7 V) fails B'; Mn couples 4.0-4.1 V.\n- Hence: Co-Mn spinel system — outside the documented layered+olivine system, per guidance.\n\n## Proposals (see log.jsonl entries 1-3 for full machine-readable records)\n1. **LiCoMnO4** (primary) — canonical Co 5 V spinel; literature true V ~5.0 V\n   (Co3+/4+ plateau, Mn4+ spectator); QE-clean.\n2. **LiCo2O4** (aggressive) — Co-only spinel, single ~5.0 V plateau (Kawai);\n   maximizes computed-V upside; stability risk flagged for stage D.\n3. **LiMn1.5Co0.5O4** (Co-poor fallback) — Co2+/3+ ~4.9 V + Co3+/4+ ~5.1 V steps;\n   literature span 4.7-5.0 V makes B' marginal; highest capacity of the trio.\n\nAll three: TM-sum = 2 (spinel dispatch), QE-runnable, Co-based (outside the\nNi-olivine guard family), deterministic capacity proxies 99-103 mAh/g computed\n(89-92 mAh/g bridged per rule C). Voltage priors are literature priors, NOT simulated.\n\n## Next stage (post-canary, only when a resumed session has an execution channel)\n1. run-comp replay on entries 1-3 -> computed (V, C, stab).\n2. comp_envelope_check.py per candidate (criterion A; expected auto-pass if B passes).\n3. B' adjudication via run-qe (candidates 1-3 are QE-runnable) + MP/catalog.\n4. Bridge rule (C) on the surviving candidate(s).\n5. Closed-loop D: full replay chain; then cell-level delivery on the Chen2020 profile.\n\nNo values in this workspace are fabricated; all simulation outputs remain pending.\n"}
